**Short Story:**  
Zizzle Sparksprocket tiptoed through Stranglethorn's jungle, his Succubus, Silkshadow, shimmering beside him. A panther lunged! Silkshadow instantly Seduced it, while Zizzle's Shadow Bolts rained down. They danced between mobs—Seduce one, burn another, vanish with Lesser Invisibility. But when two trolls ambushed them, Silkshadow’s whispers couldn’t hold both. Zizzle panicked, fumbling for a Healthstone as claws tore into his robes. *"Maybe a meat-shield wouldn’t be so bad..."* he gasped, fleeing toward Booty Bay.  

**Answer:**  
Voidwalkers are more common due to **safety and simplicity**. While Succubus offers higher damage and CC, she requires active micromanagement and is fragile. The Voidwalker’s taunt (Torment/Suffering) and shield (Sacrifice) forgive mistakes, allowing less experienced players to survive unexpected adds or overpulls—critical in Classic’s punishing world. Players prioritize survivability over optimal speed, making the "blueberry" a reliable, low-effort companion. [end of text]


